    "Scouting Notes": "Howell broke out in 2021 in High A Wisconsin. He has always shown flashes of his tools. He's a plus runner, both in ability and straight line speed. Though he still spends some time in the infield (he was mainly a SS his first couple of seasons and has recently played some 3B), Howell has now shown an ability to play all three outfield spots, and has picked them up quite well in a short amount of time. There's a chance he is a plus defensive outfielder at his peak. Howell has begun driving the ball this season, something he had not done previously in his pro career. His power numbers soared in 2021, showing exit velos on home runs of at least 108 MPH. \n\nHe started very slowly in AA after a mid season promotion, but has picked things up of late. It's a bit concerning however, that he was 20 for 23 on steals at High A, but has already been caught 3 times in 5 tries at AA. The speed is very legitimate, making me think this might be more of a lack of baserunning instinct or ability.\n\nRight now, the hit tool is lacking, so he looks more like a Keon Broxton type player at his peak. If he can find some more consistency with the quality of his contact, and cut down on his K% (currently about 34% in AA), there could still be a second breakout for Howell.",
